WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.765
Where is it? And which way? A
grid and a compass answer both.

2
00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:12.793
Eight compass points, and a
pair of numbers for every place.

3
00:00:13.293 --> 00:00:16.591
A compass always has four
main points on every map.

4
00:00:16.811 --> 00:00:20.340
North, east, south and west,
going round in that order.

5
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.136
You are facing north. Now
make a quarter turn clockwise.

6
00:00:24.356 --> 00:00:28.675
You are facing east. Each quarter
turn moves you on one point.

7
00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:33.074
A quarter turn is a right angle.
Four turns make a full turn.

8
00:00:33.574 --> 00:00:37.104
Between north and east
there sits one more point.

9
00:00:37.324 --> 00:00:41.178
Its name is both names
joined together: north-east.

10
00:00:41.398 --> 00:00:44.789
South and west join in the
same way, to make south-west.

11
00:00:45.009 --> 00:00:48.677
There are four of these in-between
points, one in each gap.

12
00:00:48.897 --> 00:00:52.612
That makes eight in all, and
north or south always comes first.

13
00:00:53.112 --> 00:00:56.131
A route is moves, one
after another, in order.

14
00:00:56.351 --> 00:00:59.509
Hodan starts on this square.
North is up the grid.

15
00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:03.676
She walks three squares east.
Count them: one, two, three.

16
00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:07.147
Then she walks two squares
north, up two rows.

17
00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:13.219
She is still three squares east of her
start. North changed the row, not the column.

18
00:01:13.719 --> 00:01:17.109
This grid has numbers along
the bottom and up the side.

19
00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:20.858
A coordinate is a pair of
numbers, like three and two.

20
00:01:21.078 --> 00:01:24.050
Go along three first,
then go up two squares.

21
00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.496
That lands on the point. Along
first, then up, every time.

22
00:01:28.716 --> 00:01:33.128
Swap them and you are somewhere else. Two
along and three up is a different place.

23
00:01:33.628 --> 00:01:37.390
A shape sits on the grid.
Every corner has its own pair.

24
00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.885
This corner here is one along and one up.

25
00:01:40.105 --> 00:01:43.217
The corner opposite is
four along and three up.

26
00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:46.595
The other two borrow one
number from each of those.

27
00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:51.505
Read every corner the same way:
along the bottom, then up the side.

28
00:01:52.005 --> 00:01:56.278
A mirror line runs down the grid,
along the edge of this shape.

29
00:01:56.498 --> 00:02:00.817
Every square receives a partner,
the same distance the other side.

30
00:02:01.037 --> 00:02:04.705
This square is right against the
line, so its partner touches it.

31
00:02:04.925 --> 00:02:08.733
This is two squares back, so
its partner is two squares out.

32
00:02:08.953 --> 00:02:12.947
All six squares cross over, and
the picture is twice as wide.

33
00:02:13.447 --> 00:02:18.695
Eight compass points name every direction.
A quarter turn is a right angle.

34
00:02:18.915 --> 00:02:23.002
A route is moves in order. A
coordinate is along first, then up.

35
00:02:23.222 --> 00:02:25.358
Every corner has its own pair.

36
00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.132
And a mirror gives every
square its partner.
